<title>JAPAN: Tokyo precious metals market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo precious metals market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo precious metal futures market is closed for a national holiday on Monday. Trading will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, yen-based Tokyo precious metals futures settled mostly weaker.</p>
<p>Benchmark October gold was down five yen per gram at 1,363 yen. Benchmark October platinum was three yen per gram lower at 1,377 yen.</p>
</text>
